  "detector_quality_diagnosis": {
    "conclusion": "The accepted unscaled FP6 format cannot store native pixel coordinates above 24. Candidate coordinate stores saturate before NMS; letterbox unpadding can then clip boxes to zero area. Class probabilities below 0.03125 also round to zero. The two native backends agree on all layers, and an independent FP32 observation of the same lowering matches the frozen model. This is an expected catastrophic outcome of this format under the strict policy, not evidence of an engine mismatch.",
